@startuml
title Sequence diagram: coordinator confirms the event
hide footbox
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center

' People work in the Web App, which calls the Backend API with their login token, so
' every call and its answer is two arrows: person <-> Web App, Web App <-> Backend API.
' Only the arrows to and from the Backend API and PostgreSQL are numbered, as in the
' draw.io and PDF versions.
' A notification is a record saved in PostgreSQL. Nothing is pushed to its recipient
' (no email, websocket or polling): the Web App fetches it later with
' GET /api/notifications, as the last section shows.

actor "Event\nCoordinator" as coordinator
actor "Event\nOrganiser" as organiser
participant "Web App\n(React)" as web
participant "Backend API" as api
database "PostgreSQL" as db

== Coordinator confirms the event (it must be in Safety Review, with every approval in) ==
coordinator -> web : Confirm the event
autonumber
web -> api : POST /api/events/requests/:reference/confirm
api -> db : Check: Safety Officer approved,\nvenues approved and booked,\nequipment outcomes recorded
api -> db : Status becomes confirmed
api -> db : Save notification: organiser
api --> web : The request, now confirmed
autonumber stop
web --> coordinator : Show the request

== Later, the Web App fetches the organiser's saved notifications (nothing is pushed) ==
organiser -> web : Open notifications
autonumber resume
web -> api : GET /api/notifications
api --> web : Your event has been confirmed
autonumber stop
web --> organiser : Show notifications
@enduml
